{
  "info": {
    "name": "MuleMart Inventory API",
    "description": "Full endpoint coverage for the MuleMart Global Omni-Channel Inventory API (all 10 RAML resources), plus key error paths (404/409/400) and status-threshold demos (CRITICAL < 10, LOW 10-49, NORMAL 50-99, HEALTHY 100-200, OVERSTOCK > 200).\n\nRun folders top to bottom. Requests include test assertions so a live run shows green checkmarks.\n\nNote: the regional CSV sync (`regional-csv-listener-flow`) is triggered by dropping a file into the configured inbound directory, not by an HTTP call, so it has no request here - mention/demo it by dropping a CSV file if needed.\n\nWatch `procurement.alert.queue` and `inventory.update.queue` in the ActiveMQ console (default http://localhost:8161/admin) during the Create/Update/Delete/JMS folders to show the JMS + Salesforce + audit-log side effects live.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8081/api" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET Health Check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Body has status/database/salesforce', () => {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('status');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('database');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('salesforce');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
